"""SOSIX POSIX code-patch leaf for the XRay stage-2 native patcher (PR5).

Design: doc/04_architecture/compiler/xray/xray_compiler_structural_change_2026-11-06.md
C.2 "Leaves (Linux)". A narrow page-range leaf, NOT an arbitrary-address API:
its only caller is XrayNativeSledLeafV1, which derives every address from a
manifest that passed trace_native_map_validate_v1.

- begin: rt_mprotect(page, len, PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE) (RX -> RW, W^X; the
  runtime rejects PROT_WRITE|PROT_EXEC outright).
- store_u32: one aligned 32-bit store through rt_ptr_write_i32 (AArch64).
- store_u16: one aligned 16-bit store through rt_ptr_write_i16 (x86-64
  activation word, PR6); load_u16 composes two byte reads (no 16-bit read
  extern exists in every lane, and quiescent mode needs no atomic read).
  rt_ptr_write_i16 is backed by the seed interpreter (where the patcher runs
  today) and the C runtime, but not the Rust runtime archive (baselined
  c-only / unbacked). A silent no-op there is caught by the leaf's re-read,
  which reports FAILED, never "on".
- end: rt_mprotect(page, len, PROT_READ|PROT_EXEC). The C runtime
  (platform/unix_common.h, runtime_legacy_core.c) follows every execute grant
  with __builtin___clear_cache over the range - DC CVAU / DSB ISH / IC IVAU /
  DSB ISH / ISB on AArch64 - and on sync failure drops the page to PROT_NONE
  and returns -1, which the leaf reports as a fault, never as "off".

Same contract under the Rust seed: since PR5b its interpreter `rt_mprotect`
runs the same DC CVAU / DSB ISH / IC IVAU / DSB ISH / ISB sequence after an
execute grant on aarch64 Linux (fail closed to PROT_NONE), so the patcher
owns a real RX page in-process there too
(test/01_unit/lib/nogc_sync_mut/trace/xray_native_inprocess_patch_spec.spl).

Quiescent only (design C.2, Q6): begin() removes execute permission from the
whole page, so the caller must guarantee no thread executes ANY code on that
page between begin and end (startup, or SOSIX-established quiescence). There
is no live-patch mode here; a Live config is refused by the control plane.
"""

use std.nogc_sync_mut.trace.xray_native_sled_leaf_v1.{XrayCodePatchPortV1}
use std.nogc_sync_mut.trace.observer_native_channel_v1.{trace_native_channel_close_v1}

@unsafe(reason: "changes page protection of a manifest-validated code page", capabilities: [ffi])
extern fn rt_mprotect(addr: i64, length: i64, prot: i64) -> i64
@unsafe(reason: "aligned 32-bit store to a manifest-validated sled word on a page made RW by begin", capabilities: [ffi])
extern fn rt_ptr_write_i32(addr: i64, offset: i64, value: i32)
@unsafe(reason: "reads a manifest-validated sled word", capabilities: [ffi])
extern fn rt_ptr_read_i32(addr: i64, offset: i64) -> i32
@unsafe(reason: "aligned 16-bit store to a manifest-validated x86-64 sled word on a page made RW by begin", capabilities: [ffi])
extern fn rt_ptr_write_i16(addr: i64, offset: i64, value: i32)
@unsafe(reason: "reads a byte of a manifest-validated sled word", capabilities: [ffi])
extern fn rt_ptr_read_u8(addr: i64, offset: i64) -> i64

val SOSIX_PROT_READ_WRITE: i64 = 3
val SOSIX_PROT_READ_EXEC: i64 = 5

export SosixCodePatchAdapterV1

pub class SosixCodePatchAdapterV1:
    pass

impl XrayCodePatchPortV1 for SosixCodePatchAdapterV1:
    me begin(page: i64, length: i64) -> i64:
        unsafe(capabilities: [ffi]): rt_mprotect(page, length, SOSIX_PROT_READ_WRITE)

    me store_u32(addr: i64, value: i64) -> i64:
        if addr <= 0 or addr % 4 != 0 or value < 0 or value > 4294967295: return -1
        # Two's-complement reinterpretation, never a saturating cast.
        val signed = if value > 2147483647: value - 4294967296 else: value
        unsafe(capabilities: [ffi]): rt_ptr_write_i32(addr, 0, signed as i32)
        0

    fn load_u32(addr: i64) -> i64:
        if addr <= 0 or addr % 4 != 0: return -1
        val word = unsafe(capabilities: [ffi]): rt_ptr_read_i32(addr, 0)
        (word as i64) & 4294967295

    me store_u16(addr: i64, value: i64) -> i64:
        if addr <= 0 or addr % 2 != 0 or value < 0 or value > 65535: return -1
        unsafe(capabilities: [ffi]): rt_ptr_write_i16(addr, 0, value as i32)
        0

    fn load_u16(addr: i64) -> i64:
        if addr <= 0 or addr % 2 != 0: return -1
        val low = unsafe(capabilities: [ffi]): rt_ptr_read_u8(addr, 0)
        val high = unsafe(capabilities: [ffi]): rt_ptr_read_u8(addr, 1)
        (low & 255) | ((high & 255) << 8)

    me end(page: i64, length: i64) -> i64:
        unsafe(capabilities: [ffi]): rt_mprotect(page, length, SOSIX_PROT_READ_EXEC)

    me close_channel(arena: i64) -> i64:
        unsafe(capabilities: [ffi]): trace_native_channel_close_v1(arena)
